        "ru-extract.jsonl": [
            {
                "entry_id": "8e3ce9fc-aa1c-32e6-a4c1-5f61f27b98f7",
                "word": "скрупулёзно",
                "pos": "adv",
                "lang_code": "ru",
                "forms": [],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "6e0a0ddb-1179-31a1-889c-8739c3f5cd81",
                        "entry_id": "8e3ce9fc-aa1c-32e6-a4c1-5f61f27b98f7",
                        "glosses": [
                            "наречие к скрупулёзный; чрезвычайно тщательно, точно до мелочей"
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "adverb"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "3613cbe2-67a4-43a7-b415-991917f7fd6c",
                                "sense_id": "6e0a0ddb-1179-31a1-889c-8739c3f5cd81",
                                "text": "Они ворошили соломенные тюфяки и подушки, скрупулёзно исследовали каждый миллиметр пола и стен."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "a6bbb740-ce4b-4524-9cee-3cf235a9e00b",
                                "sense_id": "6e0a0ddb-1179-31a1-889c-8739c3f5cd81",
                                "text": "Но для вящей убедительности Демоль скрупулёзно повторил эксперименты Нава и Грамполова, выполненные в 1942 году, причём на двух образцах эфирного масла, полученных из жасминов египетской и итальянской разновидностей."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "a496e279-63fc-49f2-9cf6-81970b74eb2b",
                                "sense_id": "6e0a0ddb-1179-31a1-889c-8739c3f5cd81",
                                "text": "Они очень скрупулёзно, по-немецки, годами перечисляют скромные авторские гонорары на счёт."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "87c35e23-2d88-44c0-8945-97cb579dec20",
                        "source_entry_id": "8e3ce9fc-aa1c-32e6-a4c1-5f61f27b98f7",
                        "source_sense_id": "6e0a0ddb-1179-31a1-889c-8739c3f5cd81",
                        "target_lang_word": "scrupulously",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "scrupulously",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "31ac0913-21d0-379a-9696-cf1af1981cf3",
                                        "entry_id": "e44a8c37-b6a8-3002-a9c3-a9439c5c79c3",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "In a careful manner, with scruple; done with careful attention to detail."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "c776fa5b-eca8-4cd4-aae3-bcfc5b89f741",
                                                "sense_id": "31ac0913-21d0-379a-9696-cf1af1981cf3",
                                                "text": "They were frightened when he threatened this, and promised to obey him scrupulously if he would but promise not to desert them."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "28dac5a7-1084-49d6-bce8-bb312a369c59",
                                                "sense_id": "31ac0913-21d0-379a-9696-cf1af1981cf3",
                                                "text": "Stock is generally well maintained, and the locomotives and railcars are kept scrupulously clean. The former are painted an unrelieved black, and the latter blue and cream, while the coaches are grey."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "2386ffab-d215-44c0-8010-5edf24db3c0b",
                                                "sense_id": "31ac0913-21d0-379a-9696-cf1af1981cf3",
                                                "text": "Some of them have, in fact, given them a theoretical elaboration which for subtlety, refinement, and elegance need make no apologies to the older economics, and which remains faithful to older theorizing in at least one respect, that the tradition of unintelligibility to the layman is scrupulously observed."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "9163279a-acb7-44d3-9b1a-96106e0b8dee",
                                                "sense_id": "31ac0913-21d0-379a-9696-cf1af1981cf3",
                                                "text": "The citizens of India and Japan have elected nationalist leaders who many say they believe champion a more closed form of identity than their predecessors. While these leaders have observed the principles of liberalism more scrupulously than the Orbáns or Erdogans of the world, their critics suspect that they are quietly fostering intolerance among their supporters."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "29ba6d84-4342-4b8d-90bf-e03a8a275571",
                        "source_entry_id": "8e3ce9fc-aa1c-32e6-a4c1-5f61f27b98f7",
                        "source_sense_id": "6e0a0ddb-1179-31a1-889c-8739c3f5cd81",
                        "target_lang_word": "punctually",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "punctually",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "455c9be0-a972-3208-8b5f-36894b2b629e",
                                        "entry_id": "07eb424b-ce70-3732-9bc7-5a9b8e46e38b",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "In a punctual manner; on time."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": []
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "6d31d704-89f3-3113-a074-f202c814543e",
                                        "entry_id": "07eb424b-ce70-3732-9bc7-5a9b8e46e38b",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Precisely; exactly; minutely."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "archaic"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "aee812e6-c056-4098-9f22-1cdbeebe9c17",
                                                "sense_id": "6d31d704-89f3-3113-a074-f202c814543e",
                                                "text": "To understand that he is not punctually right, nor those from whom he differs absolutely wrong."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "592ec15d-4ea1-4322-861a-6f90e04b7185",
                        "source_entry_id": "8e3ce9fc-aa1c-32e6-a4c1-5f61f27b98f7",
                        "source_sense_id": "6e0a0ddb-1179-31a1-889c-8739c3f5cd81",
                        "target_lang_word": "to the letter",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "to the letter",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "27da4d52-24e1-3bc6-a61f-15fdbe992da6",
                                        "entry_id": "702bc775-79e2-35a3-8b95-ca5c195aab7f",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Literally, exactly, following the rules as written."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "idiomatic",
                                            "not-comparable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "b627fffc-acc3-4094-8a05-510f5cdd8b26",
                                                "sense_id": "27da4d52-24e1-3bc6-a61f-15fdbe992da6",
                                                "text": "You should follow what your boss said to the letter. Otherwise, you'll lose your job."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "a9738d2b-2e77-43fa-a387-19e840d0c210",
                                                "sense_id": "27da4d52-24e1-3bc6-a61f-15fdbe992da6",
                                                "text": "Capello warned his players that caution was not an option as they went in search of the result that would take England to Euro 2012. And his message was carried out to the letter in the opening exchanges as England played with a tempo and threat Montenegro struggled to subdue."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "9866307d-543e-4a1c-99a6-7b4b88cf2aa0",
                        "source_entry_id": "8e3ce9fc-aa1c-32e6-a4c1-5f61f27b98f7",
